{"availability":"available","full":"lmammino/oidc-authorizer","name":"oidc-authorizer","description":"A high-performance Lambda authorizer for API Gateway that can validate OIDC tokens","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":61,"forks":11,"created":"2023-10-23T11:06:39Z","updated":"2026-05-25T15:08:22Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://loige.co","topics":["api","api-gateway","authorizer","aws","jwt","lambda","oidc","openid","openid-connect","rest-api","sar","serverless-application-repository","validation"],"demo":"https://playcel.undistro.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.303Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.303Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.303Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.303Z","stars":61,"forks":11}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A high-performance token-based API Gateway authorizer Lambda that can validate OIDC-issued JWT tokens.","This project provides an easy-to-install AWS Lambda function that can be used as a custom authorizer for AWS API Gateway. This authorizer can validate OIDC-issued JWT tokens and it can be used to secure your API endpoints using your OIDC provider of choice (e.g. Apple, Auth0, AWS Cognito, Azure AD / Microsoft Entra ID, Facebook, GitLab, Google, Keycloak, LinkedIn, Okta, Salesforce, Twitch, etc.).","A diagram illustrating how this project can be integrated. A user sends an authenticated request to API Gateway. API Gateway is configured to use a custom lambda as an authorizer (THIS PROJECT!). The lambda talks with your OIDC provider to get the public key to validate the user token and responds to API Gateway to Allow or Deny the request."],"features":["You are using REST APIs and you want to secure your endpoints using OIDC-issued tokens. For instance, if you want to build APIs that are only available in a private VPC, you are currently forced to use REST APIs.","You are using HTTP APIs but your OIDC provider gives you tokens that are not signed with the RSA algorithm (currently the only one supported by the built-in JWT authorizer).","You want more flexibility in the validation process of your tokens. For instance, you might want to validate the aud claim of your tokens against a list of values, instead of a single value (which is the only option…","You want to customise the validation process even further. In this case, you can fork this project and customise the validation logic to your needs."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"725fd9b776029db2b50c4cf2846a3d1bbd28e4060781c02c0ddac18d235c5e55","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.461Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.461Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A high-performance token-based API Gateway authorizer Lambda that can validate OIDC-issued JWT tokens.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Ideally this Lambda, should provide minimal cost, even when used to protect Lambda functions that are invoked very frequently.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Useful if you need to deploy this stack multiple times in the same account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"725fd9b776029db2b50c4cf2846a3d1bbd28e4060781c02c0ddac18d235c5e55","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.462Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-05-25T15:08:22Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lmammino/oidc-authorizer/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:33.463Z","hash":"725fd9b776029db2b50c4cf2846a3d1bbd28e4060781c02c0ddac18d235c5e55","originalBytes":185